blurb: The South Portland School Board convened its third FY26 budget workshop, grappling
  with deep cuts and debating proposals to restore critical student-facing positions
  like SEL and ESOL teachers. Amidst calls for shared sacrifice, the board ultimately
  decided to delay a final vote, seeking more time for deliberation and to explore
  alternative funding solutions.
